4-Way Traffic Light Controller Using Verilog HDL

Overview

This project implements a four-way traffic light controller using Verilog Hardware Description Language (HDL). It controls traffic in two directions: North–South (NS) and East–West (EW).

The controller uses a six-state finite-state machine (FSM) and was simulated using VeriBit Playground.

Features

- Six-state finite-state machine.
- Independent North–South and East–West traffic signals.
- All-red transition states between traffic directions.
- Clock-driven state transitions.
- Asynchronous reset.
- Simulation testbench and waveform inspection.

State Sequence

1. NS Green — EW Red
2. NS Yellow — EW Red
3. All Red
4. NS Red — EW Green
5. NS Red — EW Yellow
6. All Red
7. Repeat

