Simulation

The design was simulated in VeriBit Playground. The console output was used to inspect the state sequence, and the waveform viewer was used to observe signal transitions.

Learning Outcomes

- Understanding finite-state machines.
- Writing sequential and combinational Verilog logic.
- Using clock and reset signals.
- Reading simulation output and timing waveforms.
- Organizing and documenting an HDL project.

Limitations

This is an educational simulation. Each state lasts one clock cycle, and the design has not been validated for real-world traffic control. It does not include timed intervals, pedestrian signals, or hardware testing.

